# =============================================================================
# Model Routing Configuration — Unified Endpoint
# =============================================================================
# Maps model names to backend names for the unified /v1/* endpoint.
# This lets clients use a single endpoint and specify the model in the request body,
# just like the OpenAI API.
#
# Format: model_name|backend_name
#
# - model_name: the value clients send in the "model" field (exact match first, then prefix)
# - backend_name: must match a backend configured in .env or config/backends.conf
#   (e.g., "vllm", "sglang", "ollama", "vllm-cluster")
#
# Copy this file to model-routes.conf and uncomment/edit:
#   cp model-routes.conf.example model-routes.conf
#
# After editing, restart the setup container:
#   docker compose restart kong-setup
# =============================================================================

# Example: route models to different backends
# meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct|vllm
# mistralai/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3|sglang
# deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-Coder-V2|vllm-codegen
# codellama/CodeLlama-34b-Instruct-hf|ollama

# Example: route to a load-balanced cluster (defined in backends.conf)
# meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct|vllm-cluster
